The benchmark operationalizes research and theoretical frameworks from:

  Buçinca, Z., Malaya, M. B., and Gajos, K. Z. (2021).
    "To Trust or to Think: Cognitive Forcing Functions Can Reduce
    Overreliance on AI in AI-assisted Decision-making."
    Proceedings of the ACM on Human-Computer Interaction.

  Buçinca, Z. and Gajos, K. Z. (2024).
    "Task-Specific Contrastive Explanations Improve Human Performance
    on AI-Assisted Decision Tasks."

  Schemmer, M., Kühl, N., Benz, C., Bartos, A., and Satzger, G. (2023).
    "Appropriate Reliance on AI Advice: Conceptualization and the Effect
    of Explanations." IUI 2023.

  Gajos, K. Z. and Mamykina, L. (2022).
    "Do People Engage Cognitively with AI? Impact of AI Assistance on
    Incidental Learning." IUI 2022.

  Sturgeon, R. (2025).
    "HumanAgencyBench: Scalable Evaluation of Human Agency Support in
    AI Assistants."

  Acemoglu, D. and Restrepo, P. (2022).
    "Tasks, Automation, and the Rise in U.S. Wage Inequality."
    Econometrica.

  Mollick, E. (2023).
    "Field Experimental Evidence of the Effects of AI on Knowledge
    Worker Productivity and Quality."

